# PHP & Laravel Standards

## 📚 **Coding Best Practices & Standards**
- Follow PSR-12 coding standards for PHP projects
- Use meaningful, descriptive variable and function names
- Keep functions small and focused (single responsibility principle)
- Implement proper error handling with meaningful error messages
- Use consistent code formatting and indentation
- Follow SOLID principles and design patterns where appropriate
- Implement proper separation of concerns
- Use type hints and return types; target PHP 8.x (use `readonly` properties and enums where appropriate)
- Follow Laravel conventions when working with Laravel projects

## 🏗️ **Laravel-Specific Guidelines**
- **Models**: Use Eloquent models with proper relationships and accessors/mutators; **always** define `$fillable` or `$guarded` to prevent mass-assignment vulnerabilities; prefer explicit attribute assignment from validated Form Request data
- **Controllers**: Keep controllers thin, delegate business logic to services
- **Requests**: Use Form Request classes for all HTTP validation; use `unique` rules with ignore for updates; avoid raw `Validator::make()` in controllers for user input
- **Route Model Binding**: Use implicit route model binding; in multi-tenant apps scope binding so users cannot access other tenants' models
- **Resources**: Use API Resources for consistent JSON responses
- **Policies**: Implement authorization policies for user permissions
- **Events & Listeners**: Use events for decoupled functionality
- **Jobs**: Use queued jobs for time-consuming tasks
- **Middleware**: Implement custom middleware for cross-cutting concerns

## 🔧 **PHP Best Practices**
- **Type Declarations**: Use strict typing (`declare(strict_types=1);`) and return type declarations
- **Error Handling**: Implement proper exception handling with custom exceptions
- **Code Organization**: Use namespaces and autoloading properly
- **Dependency Injection**: Use constructor injection for dependencies
- **Immutability**: Prefer immutable objects and `readonly` properties where appropriate (PHP 8.2+)
- **Documentation**: Use PHPDoc comments for all public methods
- **N+1 Prevention**: Use `with()` / `load()` for relationships; avoid N+1 queries in loops (see performance-optimization rule)

## 🧪 **Laravel Testing Standards**
- **Feature Tests**: Test complete user workflows and API endpoints
- **Unit Tests**: Test individual methods and classes in isolation
- **Database Tests**: Use database transactions for test isolation
- **Mocking**: Mock external dependencies and services
- **Factories**: Use model factories for test data generation
- **Assertions**: Use descriptive assertion methods

## 📋 **Code Quality Checklist**
- ✅ **PSR-12 compliance** verified
- ✅ **Type hints** added to all methods
- ✅ **$fillable / $guarded** defined on models; no unsafe mass assignment
- ✅ **Form Request** used for validation; no raw Validator in controllers for user input
- ✅ **Route model binding** scoped for multi-tenant where applicable
- ✅ **Error handling** implemented
- ✅ **Laravel conventions** followed
- ✅ **SOLID principles** applied
- ✅ **Documentation** added for complex logic
- ✅ **Tests written** for new functionality